--TEST--
`Core\Test::serverUrl()` answers `null` wherever no `#[Test(server: true)]` bound a listener, which is every context but that one — ADR 0079 § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// ADR 0079 § 18's second mechanism arms one string on the *test's* own context
// and nothing else ever writes one, so a program that is not a test has no
// address to read. Rendered rather than compared against `null`, because what
// is being pinned is the reading itself: an empty string would print
// differently, and a member that invented an address would print that.
echo Core\Debug::render(Core\Test::serverUrl()), "\n";

// And the answer really is nullable rather than a `string` that happens to be
// empty: a `??` over a non-nullable left-hand side has an unreachable fallback,
// so this line is the type stated as an output.
echo Core\Test::serverUrl() ?? "no listener", "\n";
--EXPECT--
null
no listener
